<title>BELGIUM: Credit Lyonnais Belgium 1996 profit up 31 pct.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais Belgium 1996 profit up 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Belgian francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				    821 vs	628</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total (billions)    443.575 vs  443.079</p>
<p>    Net interest income		     3,615 vs    3,450</p>
<p>    Net provisions				969 vs	824</p>
<p>    Financial transaction income	    903 vs	719</p>
<p>    Gross income				5,487 vs    4,993</p>
<p>    General costs			     3,328 vs    3,221</p>
<p>    Writedows and provisions		  572 vs	651</p>
<p>    Taxes					   858 vs	493</p>
<p>NOTE  - Credit Lyonnais Belgium SA is the Belgian banking unit of French group Credit Lyonnais.</p>
</text>
